  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "own motion, voluntarily. परितापाय—mark the sense of परि; they",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "trouble in every way. शमसुखम्—शम is the same as शान्ति; comp.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "विहाय कामान्यः सर्वान्पुमांश्चरति निस्पृहः । निर्ममो निरहंकारः स शान्तिमधि-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "गच्छति ॥ Bg. II. 71; also 70, 72. It is not used in its technical",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "Vedántic sense here ( for which see Mis. sl. 2. )",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 14. ब्रह्म &c.-those who possess विवेक discrimination",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "(between what is real and what is unreal) from their knowledge",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "of Brahman. एकान्ततो निःस्पृहाः—absolutely free from all desires.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "न च प्राप्तौ दृढप्रत्ययः—(we have) no firm belief in their attainment;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "we are not sure that they would be attained. वाञ्छामात्र &c.—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "Although they ( enjoyments ) are seized only by desire ( i. e. by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "imagination ); although their possession is only imaginary.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 15. शकुनाः—birds. अङ्केशयाः-an aluk comp. मनोरथ &c.—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "for the different ways of dissolving the comp., see com. मनो-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "रथोप०—a palace built in the mind &c ; i. e. building castles in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the air.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 16. भिक्षाशनं-भिक्षया अशनं livelihood; or भिक्ष्यते इति भिक्षा (food",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "obtained by begging), fr. भिक्ष् + आ; तस्या अशनं eating, maintenance",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "on. तदपि—also goes with एकवारं, even the coarse food is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "to be had for but one meal; it is not sufficient for the two",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "meals in the day. न जहाति—In spite of abject poverty",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "attachment to worldly objects does not die out. विषया",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "न परित्यजन्ति v. l.–in this case some such word as अस्मान्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "must be supplied. But this reading loses force since there is no",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "beauty in saying that the pleasures do not leave us. It is the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "mind that must relinquish them. Hence the reading adopted",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "in the text is preferable.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 17. कविजनविशेषैः—by particular poets. गुरुकृतम्—ma-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "gnified, praised, made much of.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 18. रागिन्—one in the power of love, an amorous person.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "प्रियतमा०—S'iva and Párvati form together but one body the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "right half being male and the left one being female. Cf. देह-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "द्वयार्धघटनारचितं शरीरमेकं ययोः &c.' Intro. s'lokas to Kád. Pt. II.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
